{
  "id": "area-of-circle-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02-oq-02-oq-01",
  "name": "The k-th derivative Fourier identity ĉₙ(f⁽ᵏ⁾) = (i·n)ᵏ·ĉₙ(f)",
  "parentId": "area-of-circle-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02-oq-02",
  "status": "completed",
  "knowledge": {
    "score": 9,
    "insights": [
      "Isoperimetric (Hurwitz Fourier) lineage. Grandparent oq-02-oq-02 proves the first-order IBP identity ĉₙ(f') = i·n·ĉₙ(f); parent oq-02-oq-02-oq-02 iterates once for ĉₙ(f'') = −n²·ĉₙ(f). This child CLOSES THE INDUCTION: ĉₙ(f⁽ᵏ⁾) = (i·n)ᵏ·ĉₙ(f) for smooth periodic f and every k.",
      "This is the spectral statement behind the whole Fourier approach: differentiation acts diagonally on the Fourier basis with eigenvalue i·n, so d^{2m} has eigenvalue (i·n)^{2m} = (−1)^m·n^{2m}.",
      "Proof = clean induction on k. Step rewrites f⁽ᵏ⁺¹⁾ = (f')⁽ᵏ⁾ via Function.iterate_succ_apply, applies the IH to the smooth periodic function f' (universally quantifying f INSIDE the ∀ so the IH is available at deriv f), then peels one factor i·n with the grandparent first-order identity. Smoothness preserved by contDiff_infty_iff_deriv; periodicity preserved by parent's deriv_periodic_of_periodic.",
      "Smoothness uses ContDiff ℝ ∞ (C^∞), dodging the finite-C^k succ/cast bookkeeping. KEY API in Lean v4.26 Mathlib: ContDiff smoothness lives in WithTop ℕ∞ where ∞ = ((⊤:ℕ∞):WithTop ℕ∞) is NOT the order-top ⊤ (=ω, analytic). So `1 ≤ ∞` is NOT le_top; use `hf.of_le (by exact_mod_cast le_top)` (mathlib's own idiom). ∞ notation is `open scoped ContDiff`. ContDiff.iterate_deriv / contDiff_infty_iff_deriv / contDiff_infty (↔ ∀n:ℕ, ContDiff n) are the smooth-deriv toolkit.",
      "Corollaries: fourierCoeffOn_deriv2_smooth recovers the parent's −n² as k=2 ((I·n)²=−n² via Complex.I_sq); fourierCoeffOn_iteratedDeriv_even gives the d^{2m} eigenvalue (−1)^m·n^{2m} (mul_pow+pow_mul+I_sq)."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "AreaOfCircleOQ01OQ02OQ02OQ02OQ01.lean: 4 theorems, 0 axioms (propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound only), 0 sorries. Imports Proofs.AreaOfCircleOQ01OQ02OQ02OQ02 (transitively the first-order grandparent).",
      "fourierCoeffOn_iteratedDeriv_smooth (induction engine, f quantified inside for the IH), fourierCoeffOn_iteratedDeriv (user-facing explicit-f form).",
      "fourierCoeffOn_deriv2_smooth (k=2 recovery of −n²), fourierCoeffOn_iteratedDeriv_even (d^{2m} eigenvalue (−1)^m·n^{2m})."
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE. Child of area-of-circle-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02-oq-02 (the −n² second-derivative identity). Generalizes the one-step iteration to ALL orders: ĉₙ(f⁽ᵏ⁾) = (i·n)ᵏ·ĉₙ(f) for smooth periodic f, by induction on k reusing the grandparent first-order IBP and the parent's deriv-of-periodic-is-periodic. Subsumes the parent (k=2) and exposes the even-order Laplacian eigenvalue (−1)^m·n^{2m}. All 0-axiom verified (no native_decide). Smoothness handled via ContDiff ℝ ∞ to avoid finite-order WithTop ℕ∞ cast bookkeeping.",
    "nextSteps": [
      "Parseval / energy form: ∑ₙ |ĉₙ(f⁽ᵏ⁾)|² = ∑ₙ n^{2k}|ĉₙ(f)|², the higher Sobolev seminorm in Fourier coordinates (needs the L² completeness / Parseval identity for the 2π-periodic basis).",
      "Higher Wirtinger / Poincaré: for mean-zero f, ‖f‖₂ ≤ ‖f⁽ᵏ⁾‖₂ with equality on the first harmonic, via the n^{2k} ≥ 1 mode-by-mode bound (the k=1 case drives the isoperimetric proof).",
      "Odd-order companion: ĉₙ(f⁽²ᵐ⁺¹⁾) = (−1)^m·i·n^{2m+1}·ĉₙ(f), the purely imaginary eigenvalue."
    ]
  },
